WEBVTT

01:56.741 --> 01:59.702
Look, look. It's her. See?

02:00.578 --> 02:02.163
It's Cha Soo-jung, the druggie.

02:02.247 --> 02:04.833
Why meet here? It's fucking embarrassing!

02:04.916 --> 02:06.668
What's she wearing?

02:09.170 --> 02:10.296
Taste good?

02:10.880 --> 02:12.090
Is she for real?

02:12.173 --> 02:14.467
It's my first meal today!

02:14.551 --> 02:16.886
I can hear every fucking word,
you bitches!

02:16.970 --> 02:18.847
What's with you?

02:18.930 --> 02:20.265
Freakin' junkie. Let's go.

02:20.765 --> 02:23.643
No, you girls can stay. Come back!

02:24.769 --> 02:26.312
Like I said, Detective.

02:26.938 --> 02:30.400
I may have taught her religion
and let her be my friend before,

02:30.483 --> 02:35.071
but that's over now.
Why should I meet that bitch again?

02:35.697 --> 02:39.868
That Mr. Lee can go fuck himself,
I'm pissed off!

02:39.951 --> 02:41.494
Hey, control yourself!

02:47.500 --> 02:48.751
Damn it…

02:54.173 --> 02:57.343
Soo-jung, I'd be glad
never to see you again.

02:58.011 --> 03:02.640
But that bitch called you,
asking you to work for Mr. Lee.

03:03.600 --> 03:05.768
If it were something hard, I wouldn't ask.

03:05.852 --> 03:08.187
Just do the interview and come back.

03:09.022 --> 03:10.607
Call on this phone.

03:13.651 --> 03:15.737
This is the last time, I promise.

03:18.406 --> 03:20.408
You feel a bit sorry, don't you?

03:20.491 --> 03:21.743
I…

03:22.410 --> 03:23.828
What do you mean?

03:23.912 --> 03:25.455
So you do care.

03:26.748 --> 03:29.042
She'll pick me up at Yongsan
and take me to the terminal.

03:29.125 --> 03:32.128
You're meeting at Yongsan,
why go to the terminal?

03:32.211 --> 03:34.005
If you're curious, come along.

03:34.088 --> 03:36.466
I can't go. How long will it take?

03:36.549 --> 03:38.301
Two hours, she said.

03:40.011 --> 03:41.512
Two hours…

03:41.596 --> 03:44.432
I'll meet you at 9:00 p.m.
in the Yongsan Station lobby, okay?

03:44.515 --> 03:45.767
You know…

03:46.476 --> 03:48.937
I know everyone calls me a crazy bitch.

03:49.896 --> 03:52.232
But still, I wish you wouldn't.

03:53.858 --> 03:55.109
Crazy bitch!

03:56.277 --> 03:58.363
I really want to live normally for once.

03:58.446 --> 03:59.697
Then why do drugs?

04:00.698 --> 04:02.158
'Cause the world's gone to shit.

04:02.242 --> 04:03.409
Only you've gone to shit.

04:03.493 --> 04:04.786
Only I do drugs?

04:05.286 --> 04:07.080
Hey, watch your attitude.

04:07.163 --> 04:08.665
Sit back down.

04:10.541 --> 04:12.043
You want a hamburger?

04:12.126 --> 04:13.795
Now you ask.

04:15.171 --> 04:16.339
Come back!

04:24.013 --> 04:28.768
A day after Ewoo Shipping CEO,
Lee Hak-seung, died of a heart attack,

04:29.269 --> 04:32.563
political, economic and cultural figures
are paying their respects.

04:32.647 --> 04:34.691
After founding Ewoo Shipping,

04:34.774 --> 04:37.610
Lee supercharged Korea's economy
in the 1980s,

04:37.694 --> 04:40.697
and led national development
projects in the '90s,

04:40.780 --> 04:43.866
earning the title
of Korea's leading industrialist.

04:43.950 --> 04:45.326
For God so loved the world…

04:45.410 --> 04:51.749
However, after the doctor's statement that
there were no signs of health problems,

04:51.833 --> 04:54.460
people are questioning
the real cause of Lee's death.

04:54.544 --> 04:55.545
YOU RUN OFF? DO…

04:55.628 --> 04:56.504
PHOTO MESSAGE RECEIVED

05:30.830 --> 05:31.998
Soo-jung.

05:32.081 --> 05:33.291
Soo-jung!

05:34.375 --> 05:35.251
Hey…

05:35.335 --> 05:37.128
Soo-jung! Come on!

05:37.211 --> 05:38.588
Wake up, damn it!

05:39.630 --> 05:40.965
Soo-jung!

05:42.508 --> 05:43.760
Hey…

05:51.684 --> 05:54.729
Raise the NS, keep checking her vitals.

05:54.812 --> 05:56.022
Yes, doctor.

05:57.857 --> 05:58.983
Are you family?

05:59.942 --> 06:01.152
A policeman.

06:01.235 --> 06:02.987
I meant, are you her family?

06:04.614 --> 06:07.116
Someone needs to make arrangements.

06:07.200 --> 06:08.785
Her condition is critical.

06:09.869 --> 06:11.662
- Prepare the Ativan.
- Yes, doctor.

06:21.339 --> 06:23.257
That son of a bitch…

06:48.991 --> 06:51.077
Eight? Eight?

06:53.871 --> 06:56.165
She's going into cardiac arrest!

06:56.249 --> 06:57.959
Hey, Soo-jung.

06:58.042 --> 06:59.252
I'll do CPR.

07:00.711 --> 07:02.130
- Get out.
- Okay.

07:02.880 --> 07:05.758
One, two, three, four, five, six.

07:05.842 --> 07:08.344
- Get the defibrillator ready.
- Yes, sir.

07:24.026 --> 07:26.696
Give me your report,
and try to explain yourself.

07:27.363 --> 07:30.074
You've been on the narcotics team so long,

07:30.158 --> 07:31.576
your judgment is blurred.

07:31.659 --> 07:35.163
They told me 100 times to
form a new team, so what am I?

07:36.038 --> 07:39.917
Do you know Mr. Lee's face,
name or age? Or even their gender?

07:40.418 --> 07:43.087
You work like crazy
getting nowhere for two years, and--

07:43.171 --> 07:46.048
You use a minor as bait
and get her killed?

07:47.258 --> 07:50.428
Soo-jung was like a niece to me.

07:50.511 --> 07:54.474
I have no interest in your relation
with that girl.

07:54.557 --> 07:55.558
Forget it.

07:55.641 --> 07:56.726
You're out of your mind.

07:56.809 --> 07:58.644
I'm putting Team 2 on the case,
you're out.

07:58.728 --> 07:59.937
I'm going to catch Mr. Lee.

08:00.021 --> 08:01.063
You're fucking crazy!

08:01.147 --> 08:02.982
Then don't provoke me!

08:05.193 --> 08:07.904
Mr. Lee, that bastard, sent me a message.

08:08.446 --> 08:10.239
"I killed your rat."

08:11.282 --> 08:12.992
Fuck off, scumbag.

08:13.868 --> 08:15.620
I need to catch him.

08:18.164 --> 08:21.083
I will catch him.

09:21.852 --> 09:22.895
Hey.

09:22.979 --> 09:23.980
Hey!

09:34.907 --> 09:36.909
Which floor is the narcotics team on?

09:40.329 --> 09:41.330
Oh Yeon-ok.

09:45.084 --> 09:47.461
You walked in here on your own two feet?

09:49.046 --> 09:52.174
Thanks for recognizing me,
but that's a bit rude.

09:53.134 --> 09:54.302
You really know me?

09:54.385 --> 09:56.262
CEO of Yeon-ok Paint.

09:56.345 --> 09:58.723
Mr. Lee's guardian and power broker?

09:59.724 --> 10:02.935
You look like a thug,
but you're well-informed.

10:05.730 --> 10:07.273
You want to catch Mr. Lee?

10:08.691 --> 10:10.568
Do it. I'll help you.

10:11.944 --> 10:14.530
But you have to hide me here.

10:16.490 --> 10:19.201
I was supposed to die today, but I didn't.

10:19.285 --> 10:22.330
If he finds out, he'll come for me.

10:48.147 --> 10:51.692
They didn't even try to hide this factory.

10:51.776 --> 10:53.402
Sir, the list of casualties.

10:53.486 --> 10:55.863
No wonder we couldn't find it.

10:57.823 --> 10:59.617
Look at the casualty list.

10:59.700 --> 11:01.410
Everyone's here.

11:01.494 --> 11:04.080
It was a meeting
with all the major executives.

11:04.872 --> 11:06.165
All dead, right?

11:06.248 --> 11:09.502
Ammonium nitrate bomb, with a detonator.

11:09.585 --> 11:10.586
You see?

11:11.170 --> 11:12.421
2007, 2012.

11:12.505 --> 11:15.674
Those two explosions in Incheon, remember?

11:15.758 --> 11:18.886
Those were ammonium nitrate, too.
Same methods.

11:18.969 --> 11:22.098
Both those times,
it was your superiors who died.

11:22.890 --> 11:26.727
Actually, it was you who benefited,
not Mr. Lee.

11:26.811 --> 11:30.189
Mr. Lee set those bombs
to clear a path for me, it's true.

11:31.190 --> 11:33.567
He became a star when Laika caught on.

11:33.651 --> 11:35.778
That was all me, behind the scenes.

11:36.695 --> 11:38.697
Guess how much my marketing earned him?

11:38.781 --> 11:40.908
I was worth clearing a path for.

11:41.659 --> 11:45.079
But this time he tried to kill me too.

11:45.162 --> 11:47.081
So Mr. Lee is the culprit?

11:47.957 --> 11:51.210
Yeah. But this time it's different.

11:54.046 --> 11:56.632
He killed his master too, not long ago.

11:57.216 --> 11:58.384
You saw the news?

11:58.968 --> 12:01.178
Ewoo Shipping CEO, Lee Hak-seung.

12:01.762 --> 12:03.097
Dead.

12:06.517 --> 12:09.603
That captain of industry
was a drug master.

12:10.729 --> 12:14.108
I thought you meant master
like in a kung fu movie.

12:15.443 --> 12:16.444
Cuff her.

12:18.404 --> 12:20.531
Catch the rabbit, kill the hunting dog.

12:21.532 --> 12:23.159
A master in name only.

12:23.242 --> 12:25.953
Lee Hak-seung was just another servant.

12:26.579 --> 12:30.875
That famed industrialist spent years
wiping Mr. Lee's ass, then was dismissed.

12:31.750 --> 12:33.544
You get what I'm saying?

12:35.671 --> 12:39.091
Mr. Lee is the devil.

12:45.097 --> 12:46.599
In here! Go, go!

12:47.641 --> 12:49.185
Hey, what's going on?

12:49.268 --> 12:51.061
There's a survivor.

12:53.063 --> 12:54.482
I'll go there.

12:54.565 --> 12:56.484
You take this guy to a doctor, okay?

12:56.567 --> 12:57.610
Okay.

13:03.324 --> 13:06.827
We're about to enter the Chinese market.

13:07.495 --> 13:11.248
The scale is off the charts,
like Samsung-level.

13:11.957 --> 13:16.045
At this crucial time,
Lee Hak-seung is bumped off

13:16.962 --> 13:18.881
and half the HQ killed.

13:23.886 --> 13:25.304
Why'd he do it?

13:25.971 --> 13:29.558
It's a clean slate, a fresh start.

13:29.642 --> 13:31.810
So Mr. Lee's ambitious.

13:32.520 --> 13:33.521
But who is he?

13:33.604 --> 13:35.231
I don't know.

13:35.314 --> 13:36.690
Come on.

13:36.774 --> 13:40.402
The remote marketing strategy
I developed was inspired by him.

13:41.195 --> 13:43.781
He never appears in person.

13:43.864 --> 13:46.075
He works behind the scenes.

13:46.575 --> 13:50.621
Only Lee Hak-seung met him in person.

13:51.288 --> 13:55.626
Still, I may not know who he is…

13:56.210 --> 13:57.419
No smoking here!

14:03.717 --> 14:05.302
But I know his name.

14:08.138 --> 14:09.640
You curious?

14:13.102 --> 14:14.979
Now I've got your attention.

14:16.438 --> 14:18.023
This is tiring.

14:18.107 --> 14:21.026
You're not tired, you don't talk.
Shall we rest?

14:21.110 --> 14:24.446
Hey, order me some stew.

14:24.530 --> 14:27.324
I need to eat regularly,
because of diabetes.

14:28.325 --> 14:32.538
My driver's alive too,
so I told him to come here.

14:33.122 --> 14:35.749
When he arrives, have him bring
my medication from the car.

14:37.293 --> 14:39.128
As we rest,

14:39.795 --> 14:41.463
let's not waste time.

14:42.047 --> 14:44.884
The prosecutor's office
has a few items filed on me.

14:44.967 --> 14:48.220
Let's start by canceling those, okay?

14:52.433 --> 14:55.936
The survivor is Seo Young-rak. Age 28.

14:56.520 --> 14:58.772
There were living quarters in the factory.

14:58.856 --> 15:00.816
The entire ceiling collapsed,

15:00.900 --> 15:03.152
but the fire didn't catch there,
so he lived.

15:03.736 --> 15:07.323
Among the deceased was a female
factory worker, that's his mother.

15:07.865 --> 15:10.075
Yook Pil-soon, age 56.

15:10.576 --> 15:13.287
They lived there
back when it was a greenhouse.

15:13.370 --> 15:16.457
When Mr. Lee bought it
and turned it into a drug factory,

15:16.540 --> 15:19.501
they stayed on and did chores.

15:19.585 --> 15:21.211
Just one survivor?

15:21.295 --> 15:22.880
Right, no others.

15:22.963 --> 15:25.549
They're still checking the second floor,

15:25.633 --> 15:27.509
but the chances are slim.

15:28.010 --> 15:30.012
And there was one dog.

15:30.095 --> 15:32.890
Its burns were serious, so we rescued it.

15:45.194 --> 15:47.112
She's a snake.

15:51.241 --> 15:54.620
Junkies look up to Mr. Lee,
like he's Steve Jobs or something.

15:55.412 --> 15:57.206
That's her doing too, I guess?

15:58.332 --> 16:01.752
There are a lot of rumors
that Lee Hak-seung was murdered.

16:01.835 --> 16:05.297
Given his medical history, there's
no reason he'd have a heart attack.

16:05.881 --> 16:08.008
Was he really killed by Mr. Lee?

16:08.092 --> 16:10.302
If she's telling the truth, maybe.

16:11.387 --> 16:13.764
Or maybe she's toying with us.

16:13.847 --> 16:15.683
But check up on Lee Hak-seung.

16:38.998 --> 16:42.751
She took the pills and ate,
is it really diabetic shock?

16:45.462 --> 16:47.756
- The driver brought the pills?
- Yeah.

16:48.507 --> 16:49.675
Check up on him.

16:49.758 --> 16:50.801
Right away.

17:01.854 --> 17:03.439
You said he was unconscious.

17:03.522 --> 17:06.275
He was. I stepped out
for, like, three minutes?

17:06.358 --> 17:07.776
And then he was gone.

17:08.318 --> 17:10.904
The doctor said it'd be a while
before he woke up.

17:10.988 --> 17:13.657
Contact hospital security
and close off the exits.

17:14.241 --> 17:15.576
We can't lose him.

17:15.659 --> 17:17.161
He's the only one left.

17:20.122 --> 17:21.832
Wait. Play it back.

17:28.505 --> 17:31.175
He's unlikely to retrace his steps,

17:31.258 --> 17:33.802
so we can rule out the emergency room.

17:34.845 --> 17:37.306
He'll be looking for some way
out of the building.

17:37.389 --> 17:40.309
Have a security guard
stationed at each restroom.

17:40.392 --> 17:42.895
I found him on the hallway security cam,

17:43.687 --> 17:45.606
but not after that.

17:58.619 --> 18:01.497
Is there anywhere
in the hospital with no cams?

18:36.240 --> 18:40.035
His mother's personal effects.
He won't even look at them.

18:41.370 --> 18:42.830
He hasn't spoken a word.

18:42.913 --> 18:45.916
He was carrying these two phones.

18:45.999 --> 18:47.751
He received a message just now.

18:48.377 --> 18:50.212
Doesn't look like spam.
Probably a password?

18:50.295 --> 18:51.839
PRE-APPROVED LOANS!
MESSAGE # 3264-323068

18:51.922 --> 18:53.924
- And the drug test?
- Negative.

19:01.765 --> 19:03.058
Seo Young-rak.

19:04.059 --> 19:06.895
I hear your mother called you Rak.

19:06.979 --> 19:09.064
Mind if I call you that?

19:09.773 --> 19:11.316
Who is Mr. Lee?

19:15.320 --> 19:16.321
All right.

19:17.739 --> 19:21.743
Still, you must know people
a couple levels above you.

19:25.080 --> 19:26.623
You won't talk?

19:27.708 --> 19:30.711
You haven't said a word yet.
For whose sake?

19:34.339 --> 19:37.217
Sure, if you were raised
by an organization your whole life,

19:37.301 --> 19:39.428
you'd be blindly loyal to them.

19:40.304 --> 19:44.141
But in the end, your mother's dead
and you were almost killed.

19:44.224 --> 19:47.811
All because of a boss you've never seen.

19:48.312 --> 19:50.063
I feel bad for you.

19:50.981 --> 19:54.443
Loyal as a dog. Oh, one dog survived.

19:54.526 --> 19:58.113
He's covered in blood but still
wags his tail in front of people.

19:58.822 --> 20:00.490
Is the dog all right?

20:03.076 --> 20:04.912
They sent a photo.

20:04.995 --> 20:08.457
Here it is. Wow, what cruel bastards.

20:09.208 --> 20:13.837
We moved him to the hospital.
Hey, how's the dog?

20:13.921 --> 20:18.717
His burns are pretty bad,
so they can't do surgery yet.

20:18.800 --> 20:20.844
They're doing emergency care now.

20:20.928 --> 20:22.596
He's in a lot of pain,

20:22.679 --> 20:25.849
so they gave him painkillers
and are trying to save him.

20:26.350 --> 20:27.351
Okay!

20:28.769 --> 20:29.895
Let's go.

20:48.705 --> 20:50.249
What's his name?

20:54.461 --> 20:55.629
Jindo Dog.

20:58.090 --> 20:59.591
It's not a Jindo breed.

21:01.843 --> 21:05.389
His throat was crushed,
so they had to open it up again.

21:05.472 --> 21:07.933
He'll still be able to eat,

21:08.725 --> 21:10.602
but not bark.

21:13.105 --> 21:15.482
Was it really Mr. Lee who did this?

21:16.066 --> 21:19.069
He's got a history of cleaning out
his board with similar methods.

21:19.653 --> 21:24.866
Someone gets on his nerves, he takes
them out, whether it's family or a dog.

21:24.950 --> 21:26.159
Like somebody once said,

21:27.411 --> 21:28.912
Mr. Lee is the devil.

21:34.418 --> 21:36.128
Can you catch him?

21:36.878 --> 21:38.171
I can.

21:46.763 --> 21:47.764
How?

21:48.849 --> 21:52.311
Nobody knows who he is. You don't either.

21:57.357 --> 21:58.734
I'm going to catch him.

22:06.742 --> 22:10.245
Over the years, several people
have claimed to be Mr. Lee.

22:11.204 --> 22:13.498
They'd bad-mouth and suspect each other,

22:14.624 --> 22:17.044
so there were a few fights at the factory.

22:17.878 --> 22:20.172
A guy who worked with me
got his hand cut off.

22:20.255 --> 22:23.717
So that's why he wanted to wipe them out.

22:24.509 --> 22:26.762
Even knowing that
you and the dog were there.

22:26.845 --> 22:27.846
No.

22:27.929 --> 22:29.514
Nobody knew I was there.

22:30.140 --> 22:32.768
I came back from a trip
earlier than expected.

22:35.062 --> 22:36.229
Here they are.

22:36.313 --> 22:39.191
So these two phones are both yours?

22:39.274 --> 22:40.275
One's a company phone--

22:40.358 --> 22:42.778
The other is for contacting
Chinese buyers.

22:43.445 --> 22:45.238
You contact the Chinese buyers?

22:45.322 --> 22:46.615
Yeah.

22:50.410 --> 22:51.912
ASCII code.

22:51.995 --> 22:54.623
Tomorrow at 8:00 p.m., Acre Hotel Suite,

22:55.957 --> 22:58.460
I'm supposed to take the director
to meet the buyer.

23:03.465 --> 23:05.592
Mr. Lee's entry into China.

23:06.343 --> 23:07.969
- This is it?
- Yes.

23:09.763 --> 23:11.765
But Mr. Lee won't show up.

23:11.848 --> 23:17.395
But the Chinese buyer made it
a condition to meet Mr. Lee in person.

23:18.855 --> 23:21.733
This buyer has top quality raw materials.

23:21.817 --> 23:24.778
Tomorrow, I need to get him
to agree to supply us.

23:24.861 --> 23:28.323
Then we make drugs with it,
go back to the buyer,

23:28.406 --> 23:29.991
and complete the deal.

23:30.075 --> 23:33.120
So Mr. Lee only shows up at the end.

23:34.246 --> 23:36.164
Did you tell the company you came back?

23:36.248 --> 23:37.499
Not yet.

23:37.582 --> 23:38.625
Then you…

23:39.960 --> 23:44.297
You're still in China,
and you haven't heard from the buyer yet.

23:45.882 --> 23:49.136
We've got 18 hours. Go brush your teeth.

23:50.095 --> 23:51.596
We're pulling an all-nighter.

24:01.148 --> 24:02.149
Look at me.

24:21.209 --> 24:22.752
MR. LEE

24:32.429 --> 24:33.722
Buyer, Jin Ha-rim.

24:34.681 --> 24:37.809
He's Chinese,
but was born in Mokpo, Korea.

24:38.435 --> 24:40.478
That's the nickname he uses in Korea.

24:40.562 --> 24:44.274
Recently Jilin emerged
as China's biggest drug market.

24:44.357 --> 24:46.735
The true market size is unknown.

24:46.818 --> 24:50.155
People say he controls
over half the drug market in Jilin.

24:51.114 --> 24:53.241
Hundreds of millions in cash,

24:53.325 --> 24:54.743
impossible to trace.

24:55.410 --> 24:58.747
He leaves no record of himself anywhere.

25:02.626 --> 25:07.464
Suddenly Mr. Lee sends him a sample,
asks him if he wants in.

25:09.299 --> 25:13.845
Jin Ha-rim was stunned
that Mr. Lee even knew about him.

25:16.139 --> 25:18.183
An answer came back that night.

25:18.892 --> 25:21.853
That he was coming to Seoul
to meet Mr. Lee.

25:23.021 --> 25:25.023
The one going to meet him
is Park Sun-chang.

25:25.106 --> 25:26.733
An original member of Laika.

25:26.816 --> 25:28.944
The organization's been cleaned out
a few times, right?

25:29.027 --> 25:31.321
The fact he survived
shows how ruthless he is.

25:31.404 --> 25:34.366
He used to be managing director
at Hankuk Airlines.

25:34.449 --> 25:38.453
With his corporate background,
he's efficient, has a good reputation.

25:38.536 --> 25:41.331
During the fight at the factory last year,

25:41.414 --> 25:43.416
he took out his knife

25:44.084 --> 25:45.961
and further secured his position.

25:46.044 --> 25:48.838
The buyer's never met Jin Ha-rim?

25:48.922 --> 25:51.132
Hardly anyone has.

25:51.216 --> 25:53.051
Then Jin Ha-rim has never seen him.

25:53.134 --> 25:55.553
I'm supposed to introduce them today.

26:05.522 --> 26:08.233
Tell Park Sun-chang
the meeting's postponed an hour,

26:08.316 --> 26:11.778
and the deal with Jin Ha-rim
is at 8:00 p.m. as scheduled.

26:12.862 --> 26:15.365
We will direct this deal.

26:15.907 --> 26:17.325
According to our script.

26:20.787 --> 26:22.497
We'll meet him first.

26:56.156 --> 26:57.824
They're here.

27:08.793 --> 27:10.170
I thought we changed them all?

27:10.253 --> 27:12.380
We did. Did you miss one?

27:18.970 --> 27:20.263
Hello, sir.

27:24.059 --> 27:25.727
Pleasure to meet you. I'm Park Sun-chang.

27:28.480 --> 27:29.481
It's an honor.

27:54.047 --> 27:56.800
Sir, we'll wait in the other room.

28:24.786 --> 28:26.037
He's here.

28:39.509 --> 28:41.010
Who are you?

28:41.094 --> 28:43.179
I'm the one scheduled to…

28:45.765 --> 28:47.016
Are you Mr. Lee?

28:48.601 --> 28:50.895
No, I'm…

28:54.315 --> 28:56.401
I came to see Mr. Lee.

28:58.111 --> 29:01.239
We'll make the products
from your materials,

29:01.322 --> 29:03.324
then he'll bring them directly to you.

29:14.711 --> 29:15.712
Thank you.

29:17.255 --> 29:19.632
Our organization has its own procedures.

29:23.845 --> 29:26.681
You know what it means
that I came to Seoul?

29:30.393 --> 29:32.145
I spend my life only in my house.

29:33.646 --> 29:34.981
I don't do travel.

29:36.941 --> 29:40.487
When I go out, things get on my nerves.

29:42.947 --> 29:44.699
The worst of all…

29:47.660 --> 29:49.287
are LED light bulbs.

29:49.954 --> 29:51.164
They're so loud.

29:52.582 --> 29:54.000
They give me headaches.

30:02.467 --> 30:04.177
I came to Seoul.

30:05.720 --> 30:06.971
Where is Mr. Lee?

30:18.066 --> 30:19.859
Fucking hell, I thought
you were some nobody.

30:19.943 --> 30:21.444
Who the hell are you?

30:22.654 --> 30:25.114
My seat was right next to Lee Min-ho!

30:25.198 --> 30:26.950
Did you take a picture?

30:27.909 --> 30:28.868
See?

30:28.952 --> 30:31.287
His face is smaller than mine!

30:31.788 --> 30:34.290
My kitty's excited!

30:36.918 --> 30:39.671
I got them tickets to a fashion show
with Lee Min-ho.

30:39.754 --> 30:43.174
So they went out of their way
to come a bit early.

30:43.258 --> 30:44.384
Out of our way?

30:44.467 --> 30:48.054
When would I ever get
to sit next to Lee Min-ho?

30:52.976 --> 30:54.352
Here you go.

30:56.020 --> 30:57.230
A present.

30:57.313 --> 30:59.482
Hey, I can't see.

31:00.275 --> 31:01.484
Looks good.

31:02.944 --> 31:06.614
I don't know how to tie it.
I'll look it up online.

31:08.449 --> 31:09.450
Learn from me.

31:12.912 --> 31:14.414
Miss!

31:18.126 --> 31:20.378
You really are a beauty.

31:20.461 --> 31:24.048
With an actress's face,
but a model's body.

31:24.799 --> 31:27.552
Sir, there's an old Chinese proverb,

31:27.635 --> 31:29.554
that if one does a lot of good deeds…

31:33.266 --> 31:35.226
Models have small breasts.

31:37.478 --> 31:38.771
Are these small?

31:44.027 --> 31:45.028
This thing here…

31:52.160 --> 31:53.369
It's a fake, right?

31:54.746 --> 31:57.665
Our supplier's brother-in-law
makes these in Hangzhou.

31:57.749 --> 31:59.751
Just tell me if you ever need anything.

31:59.834 --> 32:02.170
He makes bespoke watches too.

32:02.253 --> 32:03.504
Darling.

32:06.215 --> 32:07.884
I buy the real thing.

32:08.426 --> 32:09.594
Kitty.

32:11.262 --> 32:12.680
Yeah?

32:13.765 --> 32:14.766
Attention!

32:16.601 --> 32:17.810
Spin!

32:34.327 --> 32:36.788
You loser, buying fakes.

32:47.882 --> 32:52.011
For the crime of knowing who I am…

32:55.515 --> 32:57.392
this jerk here…

33:00.061 --> 33:02.397
I could use him as dog food in Jilin.

33:05.066 --> 33:07.193
But this kid never crosses the line.

33:07.944 --> 33:09.779
That's good, right?

33:09.862 --> 33:13.366
That's what you want in an employee.

33:14.117 --> 33:15.118
Yes.

33:22.792 --> 33:25.169
Halfway is the safe way.

33:28.589 --> 33:32.927
Koreans made up that proverb…

33:35.555 --> 33:37.765
but they never go halfway.

33:39.267 --> 33:41.978
It's hot. Or cold.

33:43.354 --> 33:44.856
All or fucking nothing.

33:45.898 --> 33:48.067
Mr. Lee!

33:52.405 --> 33:54.532
Mr. Lee's a funny guy.

33:55.241 --> 33:57.201
"I'm sending a sample."

33:57.285 --> 33:59.704
"Hope we can do business."

34:03.666 --> 34:05.126
You know…

34:06.753 --> 34:08.254
Even when people know me,

34:09.756 --> 34:14.385
they pretend not to, to save their skins.

34:15.011 --> 34:16.429
You crazy fools.

34:57.804 --> 35:02.642
I could kill you right now,
and I've got nothing to lose.

35:04.352 --> 35:08.189
Actually we had an accident
at our company recently,

35:08.856 --> 35:12.151
a fire in our factory,
so things have been unsettled

35:12.235 --> 35:14.195
as we've worked to recover what we can.

35:15.530 --> 35:19.033
At the next meeting,
Mr. Lee will meet you personally.

35:19.117 --> 35:21.619
I apologize again for his absence.

35:22.120 --> 35:26.040
So this time,
I prepared different samples.

35:27.458 --> 35:30.336
The ones from last time
were our Voyager series,

35:30.419 --> 35:34.173
but this is our first hit, the Laika.

35:34.257 --> 35:36.175
If Voyager is trendy and sensual,

35:36.259 --> 35:39.554
then Laika is classic and weighty.

36:37.528 --> 36:38.613
What do you think?

37:04.138 --> 37:05.223
Sir.

37:05.848 --> 37:08.059
How should we pick up the raw materials?

37:26.869 --> 37:31.832
You think I want to do business with you?

37:31.916 --> 37:33.542
Sir, your gun…

37:34.460 --> 37:36.796
I'm just an employee on a salary.

37:37.588 --> 37:39.840
Someone needs to report back.

37:44.845 --> 37:46.555
You'll get the call.

37:49.392 --> 37:50.476
One of you two.

37:51.811 --> 37:54.897
Whether I give you
the raw materials today,

37:56.399 --> 37:58.234
or kill you both…

38:02.363 --> 38:05.491
you just wait for now.

38:18.963 --> 38:20.339
Hurry, there's no time.

38:20.423 --> 38:22.049
You go first. Run!

38:29.056 --> 38:31.559
The monitors are ready. Everything's set.

38:43.404 --> 38:44.697
You nervous?

38:47.825 --> 38:50.161
"I could use him as dog food…"

38:50.244 --> 38:52.330
- "I could use him as dog food…"
- "…in Jilin."

38:52.413 --> 38:55.082
"I could use him as dog food in Jilin."

39:00.254 --> 39:01.839
To your places, stand by.

39:03.883 --> 39:06.302
It's 8:57. Three minutes to go.

39:27.907 --> 39:30.534
Our man is here.

39:35.456 --> 39:37.166
You heard about the Incheon factory?

39:38.876 --> 39:40.920
It's a pity what happened
to your mom, but…

39:42.713 --> 39:45.091
There's a thousand heads at stake
in this business.

39:45.966 --> 39:48.094
You told the salt factory to be ready?

39:51.555 --> 39:52.556
Bastard.

39:53.766 --> 39:55.476
Let's not screw up.

39:59.855 --> 40:01.899
"Halfway is the safe way…"

40:02.608 --> 40:05.861
Let's wrap it up, people.
Dong-woo, get out of there now!

40:05.945 --> 40:07.196
Almost done.

40:08.656 --> 40:10.908
They're leaving the elevator.
Walking your way.

40:11.617 --> 40:13.369
Dong-woo, get out! Time's up.

40:13.452 --> 40:14.870
I'm going!

40:16.831 --> 40:18.332
Wait, wait, wait!

40:18.416 --> 40:19.417
Hold up.

40:20.751 --> 40:24.004
They turned the corner.
Dong-woo, hide somewhere.

40:25.840 --> 40:28.092
Incoming. Ten meters.

40:28.175 --> 40:30.219
Team, don't be nervous. Keep calm.

40:31.178 --> 40:33.806
Dong-woo, did you hide? You good?

40:33.889 --> 40:35.349
Sir.

40:36.559 --> 40:38.227
Where do I hide?

40:38.310 --> 40:40.146
Hide anywhere, you idiot!

40:41.772 --> 40:42.898
Wan shang hao!

40:43.983 --> 40:47.194
Okay, team, relax. Don't worry, just open.

41:20.436 --> 41:22.062
I'm Park Sun-chang.

41:29.737 --> 41:31.030
It's an honor to meet you.

41:32.698 --> 41:33.699
Don't smirk.

41:41.415 --> 41:44.502
Don't bother trying to charm me.

41:45.252 --> 41:47.630
I'm not going to like you anyway.

41:49.590 --> 41:52.301
Sir, we'll wait in the other room.

42:11.362 --> 42:12.863
Mr. Lee!

42:14.156 --> 42:16.283
You guys are something.

42:17.201 --> 42:19.578
Contacting me first!

42:24.750 --> 42:26.252
Where's Mr. Lee?

42:27.127 --> 42:31.757
I'll meet you first today,
and next time, Mr. Lee--

42:33.551 --> 42:39.098
Even people who know me pretend not to,
to save their skins.

42:40.641 --> 42:45.396
For the crime of knowing me,
I could wipe all of you out now!

42:48.816 --> 42:52.403
I could rip your heads off,
and I've got nothing to lose, right?

42:52.486 --> 42:53.487
Right?

42:54.613 --> 42:55.948
Yes.

42:56.031 --> 42:57.449
Drink up.

43:06.250 --> 43:08.544
But this guy's okay.

43:09.587 --> 43:11.255
He never crosses the line.

43:11.338 --> 43:13.090
It's what you want in an employee.

43:20.097 --> 43:21.849
Okay, show me.

43:25.019 --> 43:27.187
You can rest easy about security.

43:28.272 --> 43:29.773
Inside the organization,

43:29.857 --> 43:34.069
each person only knows a few others,
above and below them.

43:34.778 --> 43:36.822
So no fire gets too big.

43:37.990 --> 43:40.242
The sample we sent before was the Voyager.

43:40.326 --> 43:42.870
This is one of our best sellers, Laika.

43:44.705 --> 43:45.706
Hold on.

43:49.043 --> 43:51.712
What material did you use
to make it so opaque?

43:53.756 --> 43:55.382
Is that really Laika?

44:00.137 --> 44:01.138
Oh, sorry.

44:05.851 --> 44:06.810
Are you all right?

44:06.894 --> 44:09.271
What's with me? Gosh.

44:11.857 --> 44:13.150
It's okay, miss.

44:14.360 --> 44:16.195
I'll do it.

44:18.822 --> 44:19.823
Sir.

44:22.743 --> 44:24.453
I'll prepare it for you.

44:34.463 --> 44:37.549
These are special raw materials,
so it's the highest quality.

44:41.387 --> 44:42.429
And…

44:43.347 --> 44:45.474
I specially prepared
one more thing for you.

44:51.688 --> 44:55.859
This is a new product
designed for Chinese tastes.

44:59.780 --> 45:00.781
Director.

45:02.950 --> 45:04.660
Let's just do the Laika today.

45:05.494 --> 45:07.454
I didn't tell him
about the new product yet.

45:09.873 --> 45:10.874
Let go.

45:14.837 --> 45:16.630
Let's just do as we planned.

45:18.173 --> 45:19.967
You little fucker!

45:27.433 --> 45:28.434
Bring it here!

45:29.643 --> 45:30.644
Yes, sir.

45:40.404 --> 45:42.906
From here, one after the other.

46:18.108 --> 46:19.193
How is it?

46:27.367 --> 46:28.494
You bastard!

46:28.577 --> 46:30.037
Are you Mr. Lee?

46:31.121 --> 46:34.416
He'll come next time, I promise.

46:47.346 --> 46:50.766
I said I'd come to Seoul to meet Mr. Lee.

46:51.892 --> 46:54.895
If Mr. Lee doesn't come next time,

46:57.105 --> 46:58.690
you'll be pushing up daisies.

47:33.892 --> 47:35.143
Breathe…

47:35.644 --> 47:36.645
Sir…

47:37.688 --> 47:38.897
Stay with me.

47:38.981 --> 47:39.982
Please.

47:48.031 --> 47:50.534
I stepped out of bounds. I'm sorry.

47:54.705 --> 47:55.706
Listen.

47:57.291 --> 47:59.293
If this deal falls through, I'm going to…

48:18.729 --> 48:20.355
Is there any more ice?

48:20.439 --> 48:22.024
Bring everything we have!

48:22.107 --> 48:23.233
Bring ice, quickly!

48:23.775 --> 48:24.860
Hurry up!

48:25.611 --> 48:26.987
Pour it in.

48:49.593 --> 48:51.219
Why'd you do it?

48:51.303 --> 48:52.888
Why?

48:52.971 --> 48:54.306
Why?

49:00.187 --> 49:01.813
We have to get him out.

49:43.772 --> 49:45.232
It's okay.

49:45.857 --> 49:47.484
You!

49:49.069 --> 49:51.738
Who told you to provoke Park Sun-chang?

49:52.406 --> 49:55.200
Did you really think
we're on the same team?

49:55.283 --> 49:56.326
Sir, hold on.

49:56.410 --> 49:59.955
You just do what I tell you.
Your actions, your thoughts…

50:00.038 --> 50:01.373
What you saw…

50:04.334 --> 50:05.419
was just a dream.

50:12.718 --> 50:14.094
Don't fuck with me.

50:15.512 --> 50:17.305
You can't do anything without me.

50:21.560 --> 50:23.019
Don't kid yourself.

50:23.603 --> 50:24.855
Even before we're done,

50:25.731 --> 50:27.399
I can throw you in jail.

50:55.802 --> 50:57.637
A message from Jin Ha-rim.

50:58.263 --> 51:00.432
He'll do the deal.

51:01.057 --> 51:03.059
He's set aside the raw materials.

51:06.229 --> 51:09.524
Hey, wanker, you fucked a girl yesterday?

51:24.331 --> 51:25.999
But where will you make the drugs?

51:27.083 --> 51:28.418
The factory burned down.

51:30.879 --> 51:32.798
There's a salt factory in Taean.

51:34.216 --> 51:36.218
The quality there's the best.

51:36.968 --> 51:39.679
There are two cooks, both geniuses.

51:40.639 --> 51:43.767
The problem is they don't communicate
by nature.

51:43.850 --> 51:47.479
And after an accident last year,
they went independent.

51:49.439 --> 51:52.692
Now they only talk to me.

51:53.860 --> 51:56.112
They're no longer
with the company, either.

51:56.196 --> 51:57.781
Why only you?

51:59.199 --> 52:01.159
I'm the only one they can talk to.

52:14.130 --> 52:15.298
Hello, sir.

52:15.382 --> 52:16.508
Come here.

52:22.055 --> 52:23.557
It's okay.

52:26.268 --> 52:27.269
See you later.

52:36.528 --> 52:38.029
The sign language interpreter.

52:38.113 --> 52:39.906
- Hello.
- Hello.

52:39.990 --> 52:40.991
I'm Jo Won-ho.

52:41.074 --> 52:42.158
Kim Soo-hee.

52:43.368 --> 52:44.828
The monitor is live.

52:50.500 --> 52:52.294
Dude!

52:55.505 --> 52:58.425
You're getting handsome… fucker?

52:58.508 --> 53:00.051
Tell me everything, it's okay.

53:00.135 --> 53:01.469
He's ugly.

53:01.553 --> 53:03.054
He looks like a TV star.

53:03.138 --> 53:05.098
- Get out!
- What do you mean, get out?

53:05.181 --> 53:07.183
What's your problem?

53:07.267 --> 53:09.519
Shut up, shut up.

53:09.603 --> 53:14.399
Hey, I got this from a Chinese guy.

53:14.482 --> 53:16.151
Which Chinese guy?

53:16.735 --> 53:18.320
There's so much, your eyes will pop out.

53:18.403 --> 53:19.779
It's okay, bring it out.

53:25.035 --> 53:27.120
Wow, one, two, three, four, five…

53:30.498 --> 53:32.250
Fuck, how many are there?

53:33.209 --> 53:34.669
Two days? No way.

53:34.753 --> 53:35.837
Two days?

53:35.921 --> 53:36.922
No way we can do that.

53:37.005 --> 53:38.089
Sure you can.

53:38.173 --> 53:39.174
Crazy fool.

53:39.257 --> 53:42.886
How much do you want to squeeze out of us?

53:42.969 --> 53:45.680
I'll suck out everything you've got.

53:45.764 --> 53:47.974
What, is this summer camp?
Have some coffee.

53:48.058 --> 53:50.560
Fuck yourself. You fuck yourself.

53:50.644 --> 53:51.645
I already did.

53:51.728 --> 53:52.896
Do it again.

53:52.979 --> 53:54.773
Come on, haul these inside.

53:55.482 --> 53:57.734
Go wash your hands. I'll make you dinner.

53:59.277 --> 54:01.696
You hungry? Let's eat.

54:36.022 --> 54:37.607
Huh? What's wrong?

54:39.317 --> 54:44.072
There was an explosion at the factory,
and my mother died.

54:44.739 --> 54:48.076
But there were so many cops,

54:48.618 --> 54:51.329
I couldn't hold a funeral.

54:52.956 --> 54:54.582
Your mother passed away?

54:55.208 --> 54:56.626
Which way is north? Go…

54:56.710 --> 54:57.752
Croaker.

54:57.836 --> 54:59.629
- Bring some croaker.
- Croaker.

55:03.091 --> 55:05.218
She liked fish.

55:05.301 --> 55:06.803
Right, hurry!

55:13.727 --> 55:15.687
IN MEMORY OF YOOK PIL-SOON

55:21.192 --> 55:23.570
When our dad passed away,

55:23.653 --> 55:27.991
his mother did the same for us.
Right, I remember.

55:28.074 --> 55:32.579
When you die you have no body,
so she'll definitely come here.

55:58.938 --> 56:02.484
IN MEMORY OF YOOK PIL-SOON

57:31.865 --> 57:35.285
What, are they robots?
How can they work 30 hours straight?

57:35.368 --> 57:37.704
Hey, they're on drugs. We're on coffee.

57:37.787 --> 57:39.164
- We're back.
- We're back!

57:39.247 --> 57:40.123
Hi.

57:40.206 --> 57:43.501
Looks like the factory explosion
will be blamed on Ms. Oh.

57:43.585 --> 57:46.754
Incriminating evidence keeps turning up
at Yeon-ok Paint.

57:46.838 --> 57:49.549
And since she died,
that complicates things.

57:49.632 --> 57:51.676
Her autopsy results are out.

57:51.759 --> 57:55.180
She took a hypertensive instead
of a suppressant, causing diabetic shock.

57:55.263 --> 57:56.848
Someone switched her meds.

57:56.931 --> 58:01.561
No evidence on the driver.
He even passed a lie detector test.

58:01.644 --> 58:03.062
Mr. Lee punished her.

58:03.146 --> 58:04.147
Sir.

58:04.898 --> 58:07.525
Here's a file on Rak. Take a look.

58:41.809 --> 58:43.770
They found this in the wreckage.

58:44.646 --> 58:45.772
Who is this?

58:47.482 --> 58:48.483
Not me.

58:49.734 --> 58:51.861
Of course it's not. What are you?

58:55.281 --> 58:56.282
But it is me.

58:56.950 --> 58:58.409
Bastard.

58:59.786 --> 59:01.120
Can I have a cigarette?

59:22.809 --> 59:26.938
Every month, Yook Pil-soon received
a banana container from Hong Kong.

59:27.814 --> 59:31.734
Usually it had 20 kg of bananas
and 1.5 kg of meth,

59:31.818 --> 59:33.736
but once, there was a kid inside.

59:35.697 --> 59:37.323
I was eight years old.

59:39.659 --> 59:42.078
The year before,
the Young-rak in this photo

59:42.161 --> 59:45.164
was playing behind a truck loading
at the factory, and got crushed.

59:45.999 --> 59:48.167
They just buried him
without reporting his death.

59:49.335 --> 59:52.422
I wore his clothes and ate from his bowl.

59:54.882 --> 59:57.552
When a notice came for him
to go to school, I went.

59:57.635 --> 01:00:01.014
And I got a citizen ID as Seo Young-rak.

01:00:01.806 --> 01:00:02.807
So tell me.

01:00:03.975 --> 01:00:06.144
Does that make me Seo Young-rak or not?

01:00:19.949 --> 01:00:21.242
Were you expecting anyone?

01:00:21.743 --> 01:00:23.786
No, no one.

01:00:25.246 --> 01:00:26.873
Go in and act normal.

01:00:26.956 --> 01:00:29.876
Don't forget, I'm watching you! Go.

01:00:48.311 --> 01:00:50.313
One is Park Sun-chang.

01:00:50.980 --> 01:00:52.523
And three cars behind him.

01:00:53.232 --> 01:00:54.984
Can't see the plates from here.

01:00:57.403 --> 01:00:59.947
The ones getting out look like guards.

01:01:00.698 --> 01:01:02.075
Wait.

01:01:02.158 --> 01:01:03.660
Someone's in that car.

01:01:06.245 --> 01:01:08.915
Bloody hell, this is loud.

01:01:16.130 --> 01:01:17.632
Director Brian is here.

01:01:18.383 --> 01:01:19.550
What, Brian?

01:01:21.386 --> 01:01:22.720
Director Brian is here.

01:01:22.804 --> 01:01:24.180
That's what Park said.

01:01:25.098 --> 01:01:26.307
Brian?

01:01:47.704 --> 01:01:50.415
Say hello. This is Brian.

01:01:54.085 --> 01:01:55.169
He's not on our list.

01:01:56.713 --> 01:01:58.339
Seo Young-rak.

01:02:00.883 --> 01:02:03.094
You're angry, aren't you?

01:02:04.345 --> 01:02:07.432
You're grieving, outraged,

01:02:08.141 --> 01:02:09.350
and burning up inside?

01:02:12.854 --> 01:02:16.315
That's to be expected.
You've been through a lot.

01:02:17.233 --> 01:02:18.401
It's natural.

01:02:21.237 --> 01:02:24.282
What is your religion, Mr. Seo?

01:02:25.992 --> 01:02:26.993
Answer him.

01:02:27.618 --> 01:02:29.036
It's all right.

01:02:29.120 --> 01:02:31.998
You can start by believing in one thing.

01:02:32.081 --> 01:02:33.666
"But let him ask in faith,

01:02:34.584 --> 01:02:37.086
nothing doubting," says the Scripture.

01:02:47.180 --> 01:02:48.389
Of course,

01:02:49.557 --> 01:02:52.351
your faith may be tested right now. Yes.

01:02:52.435 --> 01:02:53.686
That's all right.

01:02:53.770 --> 01:02:55.772
I won't let you fall.

01:03:03.988 --> 01:03:06.365
You can lean on me.

01:03:07.241 --> 01:03:08.326
Okay?

01:03:20.338 --> 01:03:22.048
Did Mr. Lee give me this?

01:03:28.596 --> 01:03:29.931
Does he know who I am?

01:04:12.974 --> 01:04:14.433
How many times did I warn you?

01:04:15.726 --> 01:04:20.022
Learn some manners
before I rip your eyes out.

01:04:40.585 --> 01:04:41.878
Yes, sir?

01:04:41.961 --> 01:04:45.214
About that Seo Young-rak.

01:04:45.298 --> 01:04:47.300
My apologies for his behavior.

01:04:47.383 --> 01:04:48.926
Actually,

01:04:49.010 --> 01:04:50.928
I put some sense into him just now--

01:04:51.012 --> 01:04:54.307
His services are no longer needed.
Let's do without him.

01:04:54.390 --> 01:04:55.808
But, sir,

01:04:57.018 --> 01:05:00.646
he's in charge of all communications,
so for now--

01:05:00.730 --> 01:05:02.398
That wasn't a question.

01:05:08.237 --> 01:05:10.406
Did you find out who he is?

01:05:10.489 --> 01:05:13.659
He's the second son
of Ewoo Shipping CEO Lee Hak-seung.

01:05:13.743 --> 01:05:14.911
What?

01:05:15.828 --> 01:05:16.913
Brian.

01:05:16.996 --> 01:05:18.372
Real name Lee In-mu.

01:05:18.456 --> 01:05:20.791
He studied at a seminary in Canada.

01:05:21.834 --> 01:05:26.380
Five years ago, he was expelled
for administering cocaine to believers.

01:05:27.173 --> 01:05:30.176
In Ewoo Shipping too,
his brothers got promoted over him.

01:05:30.259 --> 01:05:33.220
- He's always been overshadowed.
- Give me the Ewoo Shipping file.

01:05:33.304 --> 01:05:34.597
That's not all.

01:05:34.680 --> 01:05:35.806
Manslaughter.

01:05:35.890 --> 01:05:38.809
Those six believers
all died of heart attacks.

01:05:39.518 --> 01:05:40.519
On the same day.

01:05:40.603 --> 01:05:42.688
Lee Hak-seung died of a heart attack, too.

01:05:45.066 --> 01:05:47.109
But his team of lawyers
is like the Avengers.

01:05:47.193 --> 01:05:48.361
Verdict is not guilty.

01:05:48.444 --> 01:05:51.530
Looks like they silenced the press.
There's hardly anything.

01:05:52.531 --> 01:05:53.658
Move over.

01:06:00.081 --> 01:06:01.707
EWOO SHIPPING, BOARD MEMBERS
LEE IN-MU

01:06:04.961 --> 01:06:07.797
"MY BUSINESS PHILOSOPHY
BASED ON FAITH"

01:06:55.177 --> 01:06:56.762
DIRECTOR BRIAN

01:07:02.768 --> 01:07:03.769
Yes, Brian.

01:07:06.564 --> 01:07:09.525
If you turn a blind eye to Rak
just this one time,

01:07:10.151 --> 01:07:11.527
I'll deal with him personally.

01:07:12.778 --> 01:07:14.405
But for now, we need him.

01:07:14.488 --> 01:07:17.074
Jin Ha-rim only trusts Rak,

01:07:17.825 --> 01:07:22.496
and the salt factory
is impossible to handle without him.

01:07:22.580 --> 01:07:24.290
If we expel him now, it could--

01:07:38.179 --> 01:07:39.638
Let us…

01:07:43.350 --> 01:07:44.727
pray together.

01:07:51.525 --> 01:07:52.777
Sir… Please…

01:08:17.510 --> 01:08:19.762
What the fuck?

01:08:22.932 --> 01:08:24.183
Mr. Park.

01:08:26.519 --> 01:08:29.772
How many times did I tell you,
no matter what happens,

01:08:29.855 --> 01:08:32.525
never come see me here.

01:08:32.608 --> 01:08:33.609
Right?

01:08:34.652 --> 01:08:37.279
If these basic rules are not upheld,

01:08:38.197 --> 01:08:42.576
then we all fall prey to disbelief.

01:08:43.869 --> 01:08:45.412
I'm sorry.

01:08:46.122 --> 01:08:47.373
I'll…

01:08:48.415 --> 01:08:50.292
fix things, and…

01:08:52.545 --> 01:08:54.046
fix things.

01:08:55.339 --> 01:08:56.340
Amen.

01:09:01.929 --> 01:09:03.055
Amen.

01:09:20.823 --> 01:09:22.449
Nice work.

01:09:31.250 --> 01:09:32.668
Take care of yourself.

01:09:37.923 --> 01:09:40.593
Okay, Jeong-il and Dong-woo stand-by here.

01:09:40.676 --> 01:09:43.804
As soon as we get Mr. Lee,
arrest the factory boys.

01:09:43.888 --> 01:09:46.891
So-yeon, you drive out first.
Duk-cheon, come with me.

01:09:46.974 --> 01:09:48.809
We deliver the products, and we're done.

01:09:50.227 --> 01:09:51.604
Let's go get Mr. Lee.

01:09:51.687 --> 01:09:53.606
- Yes.
- See you later.

01:10:05.075 --> 01:10:06.827
What, are you joking?

01:10:06.911 --> 01:10:09.163
We brought in a truckload, and this is it?

01:10:09.246 --> 01:10:10.623
That's worth $18 million.

01:10:13.542 --> 01:10:15.127
I'll be on my way.

01:10:15.794 --> 01:10:17.379
Who's that Brian?

01:10:17.463 --> 01:10:20.549
I'd heard of him,
but this was the first time I saw him.

01:10:23.427 --> 01:10:26.513
So Park Sun-chang will pick this up
at Hannam-dong, 6:00 p.m.?

01:10:26.597 --> 01:10:27.598
Yes.

01:10:33.687 --> 01:10:34.688
Wait here a second.

01:10:47.743 --> 01:10:49.954
You little shit.

01:10:52.206 --> 01:10:53.791
Lee Min-ho has a girlfriend.

01:10:56.710 --> 01:10:59.296
Why are you so careless?

01:11:31.078 --> 01:11:33.580
You Koreans sure are talented.

01:11:34.164 --> 01:11:37.876
You make great kimchi,
great semiconductors…

01:11:39.211 --> 01:11:40.629
great drugs.

01:11:42.047 --> 01:11:44.508
I'm relieved to hear
that you're satisfied.

01:11:44.591 --> 01:11:46.427
When you do business,

01:11:48.012 --> 01:11:51.390
the most important thing
is to know people.

01:11:52.599 --> 01:11:54.893
Your money, your life all depend on it.

01:11:56.061 --> 01:12:00.649
But how can you read people
correctly every time?

01:12:01.900 --> 01:12:03.319
I'm not a shaman.

01:12:03.402 --> 01:12:05.321
You know my strategy?

01:12:07.281 --> 01:12:08.741
Whoever it is,

01:12:14.371 --> 01:12:16.373
I never trust the bastard.

01:12:17.499 --> 01:12:19.918
Where were you taking the drugs?

01:12:23.005 --> 01:12:24.131
I'm sorry, sir.

01:12:24.214 --> 01:12:28.052
Our deal is tomorrow,
then where were you going?

01:12:28.635 --> 01:12:33.682
Mr. Lee wanted to personally
inspect the product first.

01:12:33.766 --> 01:12:35.601
Since it's such an important deal.

01:12:36.643 --> 01:12:37.770
That guy there?

01:12:45.486 --> 01:12:46.487
Is he Mr. Lee?

01:12:48.280 --> 01:12:49.448
No, he isn't.

01:12:50.074 --> 01:12:51.575
Right, he isn't.

01:12:58.749 --> 01:13:01.877
That guy isn't Mr. Lee.

01:13:01.960 --> 01:13:05.089
And you're a cop!

01:13:10.886 --> 01:13:13.472
You fucking assholes!

01:13:18.185 --> 01:13:19.186
Huh?

01:13:20.562 --> 01:13:22.898
Isn't that the truck that Rak was driving?

01:13:26.568 --> 01:13:27.945
Something's gone wrong.

01:13:32.449 --> 01:13:35.869
It'd be a shame to kill you two right now.

01:13:37.121 --> 01:13:40.707
On the way back to Jilin,
I'll cut you up piece by piece,

01:13:41.542 --> 01:13:45.129
and only after you're fed to the fish
will my rage be spent.

01:13:45.838 --> 01:13:48.424
Damn, what piece to cut off first?

01:13:48.507 --> 01:13:49.758
Wait just a minute, please.

01:13:50.717 --> 01:13:51.802
Save me.

01:13:54.263 --> 01:13:55.264
What?

01:13:55.848 --> 01:13:57.808
I said, save me.

01:14:02.604 --> 01:14:05.190
- Huh?
- Dying now would be too…

01:14:19.872 --> 01:14:21.206
Duk-cheon!

01:14:25.210 --> 01:14:26.295
You fucker!

01:14:26.378 --> 01:14:27.379
Duk-cheon!

01:14:39.391 --> 01:14:41.560
Duk-cheon, get up. You're fine.

01:14:50.944 --> 01:14:51.945
Fuck.

01:14:54.781 --> 01:14:56.033
Shoot, you bastard!

01:15:56.009 --> 01:15:57.386
You all right?

01:15:58.011 --> 01:15:59.179
I'm okay.

01:16:19.324 --> 01:16:20.325
Jeong-il…

01:17:16.965 --> 01:17:18.467
You shithead.

01:17:22.721 --> 01:17:25.307
Who the fuck do you think I am?

01:17:30.729 --> 01:17:32.439
Asshole.

01:17:33.357 --> 01:17:35.525
You're a real jerk!

01:17:37.027 --> 01:17:38.028
Out of bullets?

01:17:39.905 --> 01:17:41.073
What?

01:17:52.084 --> 01:17:53.210
You bastard!

01:17:53.293 --> 01:17:54.294
Stay still!

01:17:54.961 --> 01:17:55.796
Stay!

01:17:55.879 --> 01:17:57.047
Uncle!

01:17:57.130 --> 01:17:59.132
Uncle!

01:18:12.896 --> 01:18:14.356
Goddamn you.

01:18:14.439 --> 01:18:16.149
Don't you know what "Uncle" means?

01:18:23.198 --> 01:18:24.366
Don't flinch!

01:18:37.295 --> 01:18:38.380
Get up.

01:18:38.463 --> 01:18:40.632
I'm not done yet!

01:18:50.642 --> 01:18:51.643
Let go.

01:18:52.394 --> 01:18:53.311
All right.

01:18:54.479 --> 01:18:55.814
All right!

01:19:22.382 --> 01:19:23.508
Give me the gun!

01:20:42.295 --> 01:20:43.547
Rak.

01:20:44.381 --> 01:20:45.799
Call Park Sun-chang,

01:20:46.633 --> 01:20:48.885
and tell him you're running late.

01:20:52.264 --> 01:20:53.598
24 MISSED CALLS

01:20:55.809 --> 01:20:56.643
Yeah.

01:20:56.726 --> 01:21:01.356
Listen to me, there was an accident…
We lost Dong-woo.

01:21:01.982 --> 01:21:03.191
What?

01:21:05.443 --> 01:21:06.736
Dong-woo is dead.

01:21:07.571 --> 01:21:08.488
What?

01:21:15.036 --> 01:21:16.788
- Sir…
- What happened?

01:21:16.872 --> 01:21:19.583
There was a bomb planted
in the salt factory.

01:21:19.666 --> 01:21:22.460
It exploded. Those cooks set up a trap.

01:21:23.044 --> 01:21:24.296
Dong-woo died…

01:21:28.508 --> 01:21:29.676
Get over here, bastard.

01:21:29.759 --> 01:21:33.346
Why didn't you tell me
the factory boys were armed?

01:21:34.890 --> 01:21:35.974
Tell me!

01:21:38.560 --> 01:21:40.645
Since his hand was cut off,

01:21:40.729 --> 01:21:43.648
I heard he kept guns
or homemade bombs for defense.

01:21:44.524 --> 01:21:46.776
He probably never thought he'd use it.

01:21:56.828 --> 01:21:58.455
The number you have called
cannot be reached…

01:21:58.538 --> 01:22:00.582
Son of a bitch!

01:22:08.757 --> 01:22:11.426
You goddamn motherfucker!

01:22:24.689 --> 01:22:26.816
We couldn't make it on time. I'm sorry.

01:22:26.900 --> 01:22:27.943
The quantity was so…

01:22:28.735 --> 01:22:30.904
You think you're smart, huh?

01:22:35.575 --> 01:22:37.827
You think you're the only ones
who can make Laika?

01:22:42.582 --> 01:22:45.543
Anyway, you're finished.

01:22:59.057 --> 01:23:00.517
I delivered the product.

01:23:00.600 --> 01:23:03.269
I'll get a call when Mr. Lee
finishes inspecting it.

01:23:09.442 --> 01:23:13.488
I never thought
that would happen to Dong-woo.

01:23:18.785 --> 01:23:21.371
You won't believe anything I say,
will you?

01:23:23.790 --> 01:23:25.083
But, sir.

01:23:26.334 --> 01:23:27.460
You need me.

01:23:39.514 --> 01:23:40.724
Sir.

01:23:40.807 --> 01:23:42.058
A message from Mr. Lee.

01:23:48.565 --> 01:23:49.566
6:00 p.m.

01:23:51.609 --> 01:23:53.028
- The terminal.
- Terminal?

01:23:53.653 --> 01:23:57.282
Which terminal? In the Seoul region alone,
there are more than 20.

01:24:04.497 --> 01:24:05.498
Sir.

01:24:06.207 --> 01:24:07.500
You don't think?

01:24:07.584 --> 01:24:08.585
Sir.

01:24:10.336 --> 01:24:13.631
Without blinking an eye,
he got Dong-woo killed and fucked us up.

01:24:13.715 --> 01:24:15.592
But we're still going to trust him?

01:24:18.511 --> 01:24:19.679
Why?

01:24:24.976 --> 01:24:25.977
Move.

01:24:35.653 --> 01:24:36.654
Fuck!

01:24:52.879 --> 01:24:54.089
Let's go get Mr. Lee.

01:24:55.882 --> 01:24:56.883
Get up.

01:24:58.093 --> 01:24:59.385
You don't trust me.

01:25:01.805 --> 01:25:03.848
From the start, I never trusted you.

01:25:05.058 --> 01:25:06.101
It's okay.

01:25:07.811 --> 01:25:09.187
I trust you.

01:25:18.488 --> 01:25:21.282
CHA SOO-JUNG - DECEASED

01:25:21.366 --> 01:25:22.909
OH YEON-OK - DECEASED

01:25:22.992 --> 01:25:25.787
LEE HAK-SEUNG - DECEASED

01:25:33.503 --> 01:25:35.213
MR. LEE

01:25:38.800 --> 01:25:40.760
They search you
when you enter the terminal.

01:25:41.344 --> 01:25:43.471
You can't bring electronics or weapons.

01:25:44.931 --> 01:25:46.474
How many left in our team?

01:25:46.558 --> 01:25:47.559
Right now…

01:25:52.230 --> 01:25:54.065
I persuaded him to come back.

01:25:56.943 --> 01:25:58.361
We want to catch Mr. Lee.

01:25:58.444 --> 01:26:00.071
Did you eat something?

01:26:00.864 --> 01:26:01.948
This is for you.

01:26:07.871 --> 01:26:08.872
Let's get ready.

01:26:37.442 --> 01:26:39.235
YONGSAN STATION

01:26:39.319 --> 01:26:42.780
What the hell?
The terminal is Yongsan Station?

01:27:03.927 --> 01:27:05.511
Call for backup.

01:27:33.623 --> 01:27:35.041
Hello, sir.

01:27:35.750 --> 01:27:37.001
What's with your face?

01:27:49.973 --> 01:27:51.641
Sir, please raise your arms.

01:28:13.663 --> 01:28:16.082
This is our managing director, Brian.

01:28:18.793 --> 01:28:21.087
Do you always treat VIPs so carelessly?

01:28:21.921 --> 01:28:23.423
Did we?

01:28:25.550 --> 01:28:26.551
Did you?

01:28:28.886 --> 01:28:31.389
Please forgive us. This way.

01:28:32.932 --> 01:28:37.645
Mr. Park has something
to settle with Mr. Seo.

01:28:41.899 --> 01:28:42.900
Don't be long.

01:28:44.319 --> 01:28:45.320
Let's go.

01:28:48.406 --> 01:28:52.076
That's the new product
we showed you before.

01:28:53.870 --> 01:28:56.247
This is our production room.

01:28:57.081 --> 01:29:00.918
I pay each of them $1 million a year.

01:29:01.002 --> 01:29:04.464
I scouted them myself.

01:29:31.199 --> 01:29:34.202
That's the Gyeongbu train line.

01:29:35.828 --> 01:29:37.413
At night,

01:29:37.914 --> 01:29:41.334
if you look out this way…

01:29:43.044 --> 01:29:46.589
you'll find it to be quite relaxing.
I love it here.

01:29:46.672 --> 01:29:49.050
Does it suit your tastes, Miss?

01:29:49.133 --> 01:29:51.928
So, where did you take Seo Young-rak?

01:29:52.887 --> 01:29:54.180
You rubbing him out?

01:29:55.348 --> 01:29:57.016
Did you get sick of him?

01:30:10.238 --> 01:30:12.698
You think it was Mr. Lee who ordered this?

01:30:13.574 --> 01:30:15.910
I decided myself, asshole.

01:30:16.869 --> 01:30:18.496
With all my heart.

01:30:18.579 --> 01:30:22.041
I told you I'd rip your eyes out.

01:30:29.507 --> 01:30:30.800
It's going to hurt.

01:30:32.426 --> 01:30:34.554
Straight to the head!

01:30:57.910 --> 01:30:59.537
You mean, you're Mr. Lee?

01:31:01.706 --> 01:31:02.915
When I met you,

01:31:04.792 --> 01:31:07.253
I couldn't introduce myself at once.

01:31:10.381 --> 01:31:13.843
I am indeed Mr. Lee.

01:31:26.397 --> 01:31:28.608
Let's crack things open one at a time.

01:31:29.775 --> 01:31:32.612
You wanted to work in the family business,
but he refused?

01:31:33.154 --> 01:31:34.614
I mean CEO Lee Hak-seung.

01:31:36.073 --> 01:31:41.078
He wasn't overprotective, so was it,
so to speak, belief issues?

01:31:42.705 --> 01:31:46.209
In the end, persuasion was no use,

01:31:47.919 --> 01:31:49.337
so you killed your father?

01:31:49.420 --> 01:31:50.755
Stop, stop.

01:31:52.465 --> 01:31:53.758
Stop.

01:31:54.884 --> 01:31:56.010
What you said just now…

01:31:57.178 --> 01:31:59.096
That crossed a line.

01:32:05.186 --> 01:32:06.562
I know Mr. Lee.

01:32:08.272 --> 01:32:12.526
I've known him a long time.
Much longer than you imagine.

01:32:13.861 --> 01:32:15.863
I got this far by focusing only on him.

01:32:16.822 --> 01:32:17.782
You know something?

01:32:19.408 --> 01:32:21.827
If you concentrate so much on one person,

01:32:23.246 --> 01:32:26.415
some strange,
inexplicable belief rises in you.

01:32:29.335 --> 01:32:32.213
So why does something feel wrong to me?

01:32:35.383 --> 01:32:36.801
Listening to you,

01:32:38.970 --> 01:32:43.349
your words have no pretext,
no justification.

01:33:00.783 --> 01:33:03.035
My father Lee Hak-seung believed that

01:33:03.619 --> 01:33:07.623
this thing called salvation

01:33:07.707 --> 01:33:12.503
is not something that comes
from belief or faith.

01:33:13.337 --> 01:33:16.215
If a person carries an improper faith,

01:33:17.091 --> 01:33:20.011
it's the same as having
an incurable disease.

01:33:20.094 --> 01:33:22.555
So sometimes death itself…

01:33:28.269 --> 01:33:30.396
can be a method of healing.

01:33:31.397 --> 01:33:32.940
Well, anyway,

01:33:33.733 --> 01:33:36.777
since you're the one
who flipped over the chessboard,

01:33:36.861 --> 01:33:41.907
I'll just do as I please, okay?

01:33:42.533 --> 01:33:44.160
You jerk.

01:33:44.243 --> 01:33:46.329
Droning on, trying to look cool.

01:33:46.412 --> 01:33:49.290
Hiding your true colors, huh?

01:33:49.915 --> 01:33:52.460
So you all want to play hard to get?

01:33:54.045 --> 01:33:58.382
I need to check something,
so sit down and wait.

01:33:59.633 --> 01:34:03.846
You jerks, it's rude to stand
in front of a guest!

01:34:03.929 --> 01:34:05.848
Sit down, assholes!

01:34:18.778 --> 01:34:20.237
What's that?

01:34:21.822 --> 01:34:22.823
Huh?

01:34:24.575 --> 01:34:25.993
I said, what is that?

01:34:28.412 --> 01:34:30.581
Mr. Lee sent it.

01:34:36.504 --> 01:34:38.214
So you sent it.

01:34:38.297 --> 01:34:39.340
But you didn't know?

01:34:51.102 --> 01:34:52.478
Open it up.

01:34:56.607 --> 01:34:57.608
Slowly!

01:35:01.654 --> 01:35:03.531
What the hell is it?

01:35:06.075 --> 01:35:07.493
Shit!

01:35:12.331 --> 01:35:13.999
MR. LEE

01:36:31.952 --> 01:36:33.746
You demon!

01:36:57.645 --> 01:36:58.646
Hold it.

01:37:15.079 --> 01:37:16.205
Come on.

01:37:20.251 --> 01:37:22.002
Fucker.

01:37:23.712 --> 01:37:24.797
Come here, you.

01:37:39.937 --> 01:37:41.605
Don't make a move!

01:37:42.898 --> 01:37:44.733
- Hands up!
- Don't move, down!

01:37:45.234 --> 01:37:46.569
Freeze!

01:37:47.152 --> 01:37:48.195
Hurry up.

01:37:48.779 --> 01:37:49.780
Gas masks off.

01:37:50.364 --> 01:37:51.615
Off with the masks!

01:37:58.122 --> 01:37:59.540
How old are you, kids?

01:38:48.130 --> 01:38:49.131
You okay?

01:38:51.925 --> 01:38:53.927
Those bastards took Brian.

01:38:54.011 --> 01:38:56.305
- So-yeon!
- Yes. I'm okay.

01:38:56.388 --> 01:38:58.349
- You two check the stairs.
- All right.

01:38:58.432 --> 01:38:59.516
You come with me.

01:39:14.156 --> 01:39:16.450
Hello, sir.

01:39:21.705 --> 01:39:22.998
You…

01:39:24.166 --> 01:39:28.671
Did you really think
you could become Mr. Lee that way?

01:39:31.423 --> 01:39:33.050
Seo Young-rak…

01:39:45.229 --> 01:39:49.191
It figures… I almost died because of you,

01:39:50.651 --> 01:39:52.444
so perhaps you could've become him.

01:39:54.905 --> 01:39:55.906
What a waste.

01:40:12.297 --> 01:40:13.424
Hey.

01:40:14.299 --> 01:40:15.801
This is ridiculous.

01:40:28.272 --> 01:40:29.690
Nine people?

01:40:31.442 --> 01:40:34.945
Those are the ones I remember,
but there must be more.

01:40:36.780 --> 01:40:38.824
People calling themselves Mr. Lee.

01:40:42.619 --> 01:40:44.955
But I wouldn't care
if there were hundreds of them.

01:40:46.874 --> 01:40:49.418
Lying is in Koreans' DNA.

01:40:50.961 --> 01:40:52.880
Because reality sucks.

01:40:53.630 --> 01:40:55.883
That desire to be recognized.

01:40:58.761 --> 01:41:01.680
It's quite sad, really.

01:41:05.517 --> 01:41:08.020
But the rest of the impostors,
they were all but words.

01:41:09.605 --> 01:41:12.858
This is the first time
anyone's taken it this far.

01:41:12.941 --> 01:41:14.777
To be honest, I was shocked.

01:41:20.949 --> 01:41:22.493
And I'm really curious.

01:41:27.706 --> 01:41:30.459
Who is this crazy fool?

01:41:35.672 --> 01:41:36.673
Go that way.

01:41:45.057 --> 01:41:47.184
Killing Lee Hak-seung,

01:41:48.101 --> 01:41:50.229
and removing Ms. Oh was all fine.

01:41:51.730 --> 01:41:52.773
Let's just say it is.

01:41:53.941 --> 01:41:55.692
But the factory explosion…

01:41:56.360 --> 01:41:59.238
You seem to have copied my methods,

01:42:00.739 --> 01:42:02.366
but you didn't do it right.

01:42:04.117 --> 01:42:09.373
You only thought of the goal,
not the "why" of it.

01:42:20.801 --> 01:42:23.095
If you're going to do it, do it right.

01:42:23.178 --> 01:42:26.265
I spent all that time building an image
for myself.

01:42:26.348 --> 01:42:28.892
There was no sense
or sensibility in your work.

01:42:30.435 --> 01:42:33.939
That's why all your life,
your father called you an idiot.

01:42:38.610 --> 01:42:40.070
Wait a minute.

01:42:42.281 --> 01:42:43.365
Can we…

01:42:45.409 --> 01:42:46.535
Can we pray?

01:42:47.494 --> 01:42:49.496
I'll pray for you.

01:42:50.914 --> 01:42:51.915
No, thank you.

01:43:03.969 --> 01:43:05.971
I know you're a smart man.

01:43:08.265 --> 01:43:10.350
But you made three big mistakes.

01:43:12.352 --> 01:43:16.148
Ms. Yook Pil-soon,
who worked like a dog all her life,

01:43:19.443 --> 01:43:21.987
her hair was burned and stuck to her head.

01:43:25.866 --> 01:43:27.326
You know what I thought then?

01:43:30.704 --> 01:43:32.414
She should've burned quickly.

01:43:35.584 --> 01:43:38.837
So fast that she couldn't feel any pain.

01:43:44.009 --> 01:43:46.929
And then, you couldn't even kill the dog.

01:43:47.721 --> 01:43:49.473
His back is all burned,

01:43:51.433 --> 01:43:54.645
and everything from his intestine
to his anus is all melted.

01:43:56.688 --> 01:43:59.858
He lived and suffered through all that.

01:44:05.822 --> 01:44:07.866
But your worst mistake…

01:44:09.493 --> 01:44:13.747
was thinking you could replace me.

01:44:16.208 --> 01:44:20.170
The nerve to pretend you were Mr. Lee
in front me.

01:44:28.428 --> 01:44:29.554
Are you scared?

01:44:36.436 --> 01:44:37.437
You're scared?

01:44:40.732 --> 01:44:42.859
Are you scared, asshole?

01:45:01.211 --> 01:45:02.629
MR. LEE

01:45:07.384 --> 01:45:10.053
I told you before. I trust you.

01:45:10.887 --> 01:45:11.972
So you caught him.

01:45:14.516 --> 01:45:15.517
You…

01:45:16.768 --> 01:45:18.854
Mr. Lee is going to the lobby.

01:45:46.048 --> 01:45:47.049
Out of the way!

01:45:47.132 --> 01:45:48.133
Out of the way.

01:46:09.112 --> 01:46:10.113
Laika.

01:46:21.833 --> 01:46:22.834
What's its name?

01:46:24.336 --> 01:46:25.337
Jindo Dog.

01:46:25.879 --> 01:46:27.464
It's not a Jindo breed.

01:46:31.718 --> 01:46:33.220
Why did you call it Jindo Dog?

01:46:33.804 --> 01:46:35.013
The breed isn't Jindo.

01:46:40.310 --> 01:46:41.478
I like Jindos.

01:47:10.674 --> 01:47:11.675
Jindo Dog!

01:47:12.175 --> 01:47:13.176
Hey.

01:47:14.344 --> 01:47:16.096
Hey, Jindo Dog!

01:47:24.020 --> 01:47:25.397
Laika.

01:47:38.577 --> 01:47:41.121
…then Sun-chang says,

01:47:42.914 --> 01:47:47.002
"If this is it, I've had a decent life."

01:47:49.004 --> 01:47:50.255
Fucking idiot.

01:48:01.057 --> 01:48:04.477
Mr. Lee and his gang were arrested,

01:48:04.561 --> 01:48:07.189
and a total $30 million worth of drugs,

01:48:07.272 --> 01:48:10.650
including 20 kg of Laika, were seized.

01:48:10.734 --> 01:48:13.486
The suspect Lee,
who went by the name Mr. Lee,

01:48:13.570 --> 01:48:16.573
is an heir to a prominent shipping group.

01:48:16.656 --> 01:48:20.619
Lee's organization set up
a gigantic drug production

01:48:20.702 --> 01:48:23.246
and distribution operation…

01:48:27.250 --> 01:48:29.044
Front page on the economics paper too.

01:48:29.628 --> 01:48:31.504
I said in the report
that it's not Mr. Lee.

01:48:31.588 --> 01:48:33.882
He confessed!

01:48:34.466 --> 01:48:36.927
No, it was false representation.

01:48:37.010 --> 01:48:41.348
Let's see…
How long have we worked together?

01:48:41.431 --> 01:48:43.141
Thirteen years?

01:48:44.392 --> 01:48:46.061
How come you still have no sense?

01:48:47.145 --> 01:48:48.730
- Come on.
- What?

01:48:48.813 --> 01:48:50.649
That dealer who took you for a ride?

01:48:50.732 --> 01:48:52.651
You don't even know his name.

01:48:53.568 --> 01:48:56.571
Or if he's a Chink or a Jap, even.

01:48:57.280 --> 01:48:59.866
The Mr. Lee who confessed
called himself Mr. Lee.

01:48:59.950 --> 01:49:03.286
But actually the real one
was the guy who hung out with the cops.

01:49:03.370 --> 01:49:06.122
We don't know his name or nationality,
but we'll catch him!

01:49:06.206 --> 01:49:07.374
Is that it?

01:49:07.457 --> 01:49:08.750
That's your truth?

01:49:09.251 --> 01:49:12.879
What I need is resolution,
not determination!

01:49:12.963 --> 01:49:15.131
- So that's it.
- What now?

01:49:15.715 --> 01:49:17.342
I wondered what they meant.

01:49:19.386 --> 01:49:21.846
"The world's gone to shit, so I do drugs."

01:49:21.930 --> 01:49:23.765
What are you talking about?

01:49:25.100 --> 01:49:25.934
Huh?

01:49:27.227 --> 01:49:28.353
Where are you going?

01:49:28.937 --> 01:49:30.188
To find a dog.

01:49:38.071 --> 01:49:41.574
Sir, we're reorganizing our files now.

01:49:42.575 --> 01:49:44.536
Let's start over from the beginning.

01:49:45.120 --> 01:49:47.122
The case is closed. It's over.

01:49:48.748 --> 01:49:51.960
Why don't you go shower
and get some sleep?

01:49:55.005 --> 01:49:56.006
Sometimes,

01:49:56.881 --> 01:49:59.551
when you chase something like hell,

01:50:00.176 --> 01:50:04.139
you wonder, what am I chasing and why?

01:50:06.224 --> 01:50:07.225
At times like that,

01:50:08.184 --> 01:50:10.895
just go wash up and get some sleep.

01:50:19.738 --> 01:50:24.326
I just hope you all never feel jaded.

01:50:30.373 --> 01:50:31.416
Good work, everyone.

01:52:28.491 --> 01:52:29.826
Laika!

01:53:20.335 --> 01:53:24.631
A GPS on Laika… What were you thinking?

01:53:26.925 --> 01:53:28.510
That I might not find you.

01:53:32.972 --> 01:53:34.641
Do you believe in yourself?

01:53:39.521 --> 01:53:41.356
Then how'd you make it all the way here?

01:53:45.193 --> 01:53:46.194
Good question.

01:53:49.781 --> 01:53:51.241
You're a good person.

01:53:56.037 --> 01:53:57.664
But Mr. Lee is dead.

01:53:58.498 --> 01:53:59.832
Yes, officially.

01:54:01.042 --> 01:54:02.085
But you're still alive.

01:54:09.342 --> 01:54:10.343
So?

01:54:13.137 --> 01:54:14.138
Who am I?

01:54:20.228 --> 01:54:21.854
I don't even know who I am.

01:54:27.068 --> 01:54:28.695
The container I came in.

01:54:30.655 --> 01:54:32.156
My parents were in it, too.

01:54:36.494 --> 01:54:38.955
On the way over, they overdosed and died.

01:54:40.832 --> 01:54:42.083
Both of them.

01:54:43.585 --> 01:54:44.586
In front of me.

01:54:55.680 --> 01:54:56.931
What will you do now?

01:55:09.652 --> 01:55:10.653
Want some coffee?

01:56:19.931 --> 01:56:22.100
Have you ever been happy in your life?
